        "answer": {
          "short": "$5(3x-2)(x+1)$",
          "worked": "After taking out $5$, find two numbers with product $3(-2)=-6$ and sum $1$: $3$ and $-2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}15x^2+5x-10&=5(3x^2+x-2)\\\\15x^2+5x-10&=5(3x^2+3x-2x-2)\\\\15x^2+5x-10&=5\\bigl(3x(x+1)-2(x+1)\\bigr)\\\\15x^2+5x-10&=5(3x-2)(x+1)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$12x^2+23x+10$",
